throne and nothing seems to be healing  these wounds it really becomes a  metaphor for how the throne is both  literally and figuratively killing him  in what i found to be the most  disturbing scene of this episode was the  king and 12 year old lena's walk through  the garden the king can easily see that  this poor girl has been coached by her  parents on what to say we'll later find  out that rhaenys hates this match too  seeing your 12 year old wed to an old  man who's your cousin isn't exactly  every mom's dream unless of course we're  watching an episode of honey boo boo she  even had to tell her daughter that she  likely wouldn't have to bed him until  she was 14. creepiness aside there's  some interesting talk of dragons here  mainly that of vegar for those of you  who have read the books you'll know why  this is important and why elena is  bringing this up veigar's whereabouts  are currently unknown but rumor suggests  she lives somewhere on the coast of the  narrow sea renis and rhaenyra have a  rocky relationship there's probably some  resentment here from the queen who never  was since rhaenyra will have the chance  to be queen when she never did but  renese's warnings however biting they  may be are practical the king will be  forced to wed likely have a male child  and that child will become king even  though lords from across the realm swore  fealty to her rhaenys reminds ranira men  would sooner put the round to the torch  and see a woman ascend the iron throne  at dinner both viserys and alison are  nervous viserys plays with his food and  alcent picks at her fingernails we saw  her do this multiple times including at  the tournament last episode alicent has  a special gift no it's not her virginity  it's something even better his repaired  dragon although i was joking about the  virginity thing it's heavily implied  that before otto goes off to dragonstone  that he instructs his daughter that  tonight is the night for her to make a  move in the king's bedchamber she is  super nervous about this as you can tell  by her fingernails which otto remarks on  otto is oblivious to the anxiety and  stress he is putting on his daughter an  emergency small council meeting is  called where a dragon tamer reports that  prince damon has taken a dragon egg from  the dragon pit the dragon tamer refers  to it being stolen during the hour of  the bat in the world of game of thrones  there are several of these named hours  with that of the bat being a just after  sunset missoria is with child and as is  tradition the egg will be put in the  cradle for this future targaryen  rhaenyra wants to know which egg her  uncle took and it just so happens to be  the same one that was chosen for her  brother's cradle this is an egg from  dream fire who we haven't yet seen in  the show with it being deemed unsafe for  the king to ride off to dragonstone otto  along with sir harold westerling and  kristen cole confront the prince he is  to relinquish the egg disband his army  composed of loyal gold cloaks banish  massaria and leave a dragonstone but  damon doesn't give up that easily he  even calls sir kristen sir crispin in  demon's mind he hasn't done anything  wrong he has the right to take a new  wife it's tradition to take an egg for  his child and dragonstone is the home of  his ancestors there is this great line  where daemon proclaims that massari is  to be his wife but she looks to him like  i never knew that as we'll soon realize  both the wife and child claim were a  complete bluff the standoff appears to  be at a standstill until renera arrives  on her dragon cyrax she reminds her  uncle that dragonstone is hers and that  if he wants it for himself and to be  restored as heir he'll need to kill her  of course damon's not a monster and he  stands down throwing the egg to raniera  as if it's nothing it's important to  note here that the writers aren't trying  to portray damon as a senseless monster  there is some humanity to him and he  does love his family damon's a  complicated guy but he's not a monster i  mean this is his family he does love his  family particularly loves rhaenyra i  actually think rainer earned a lot of  respect from her uncle here remember  that damon thinks his brother is weak  and renera showing this amount of  strength proves that she'd one day make  a great queen as rhaenyra flies off on  her dragon we get this brief shot of  otto who's like uh oh this could become  a problem mysteria tears into daemon  about what just happened her entire life  she's been a pawn of men and thought  being with damon would be different  using her as part of his lies has only  confirmed that damon is just like the  rest of them massaria tells him that she  quote insured long ago that i would  never be threatened by childbirth which  i took to mean that she did something so  she could never have children in the  books she actually is pregnant with  damon's child but loses it during a  storm on the narrow sea after being  forced to return to her home perhaps  this change was done to show just how  duplicitous and cunning damon is so i'm  really curious where damon's  relationship with massari will go after  this big difference from the book with  missouri's statement that she hoped  damon would liberate her from fear it'll  be interesting to see what he plans to  do to rectify this relationship in a  special meeting with lionel strong  master of laws the king gets his opinion  on who to wed lena in strong's opinion  is the clear choice while the scene  doesn't offer anything really new about  viserys's options it does reinforce how  difficult a decision this is and how  almost everyone around him supports it  minus otto of course who never  explicitly states an opinion on the  matter this will be viserys's second  huge decision that will go against what  the other lords of the realm would want  the first being his decision to name a  female as heir rhaenyra is brought to  her father to answer for her dangerous  antics at dragonstone notice here that  she is now being guarded by sir kristen  cole viserys was dreadfully worried  about his daughter his only heir and for  the first time in months the two  actually have a beneficial conversation  where they each talk about their  feelings and how emma's death has  affected them viserys tells her that  emma's absence is like a wound that will  never heal an apt analogy considering he  now has two physical wounds that won't  heal the most important line here  however is that viserys has no intention  on replacing rhaenyra as heir which i  implied as meaning even if the king does  have a male heir with a new queen that  renera will still become queen this  obviously will ruffle a lot of feathers  should this play out the scene ends with  ronira understanding that the king's  first duty is to the realm and she's  fine with him taking on a new wife the  king overlooks his realm the weight of  the decision he's about to make clearly  on his mind he has chosen alicent as his  queen and to mary before spring ends it  seems otto's plot to position his  daughter near the king during his  greatest time of need has paid off of  course corliss is pissed and leaves  before he says anything that could get  his head chopped off so too does  rhaenyra both her father and best friend  never told her about any of this for  rhaenyra it's got to feel like a  betrayal and now her best friend is  going to become her mom at what is  likely driftmark the home of house  valerian corliss has a secret meeting  with prince damon you can see just how  close driftmark is to dragonstone it  would have been a quick flight for the  prince to make corliss talks about how  the valyrians have a greater claim to  westeros arriving there even before the  targaryens but the targaryens had  something that always made them superior  the dragons he propositions damon to  join forces and venture to the  stepstones to take on crab feeder it's a  mutually beneficial alliance corliss  gets to protect his vital shipping lanes  and daemon can prove his worth to anyone  who may doubt it the episode ends with  this great juxtaposition of crab feeder  and daemon hinting at the clash of these  two princes to come now there's still a  lot to talk about in regards to this  episode and my plan is if hbo releases a  promo video for next episode for me to  do a breakdown of that where i'll  include the book spoilers you'll want to  be subscribed with the bell on to be  notified as soon as that drops thanks  for watching everyone be sure to like  and subscribe and for more bad takes you  can follow me on twitter and instagram  at thingstoryt until next time remember  it's a crispin wasn't it
 

